vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nDelegating the search test investigation to a subagent while I look at the rest.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\nThe whole suite passes now: `python3 -m unittest` runs 16 tests with no failures. Before, it ran 15, but one of those was just the failed import of `test_search.py`. Now that file loads and its 2 tests run. I didn't change any tests.\n\nI gave the `test_search.py` investigation to a subagent, which found the only problem there was a bad import. I tracked each fix in the todo list. The fixes:\n\n1. **`catalog/search.py:3`**: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`). It now imports it from `catalog.text`.\n2. **`catalog/books.py:22`**: `parse_book` kept the year as a string. It now converts it to an `int`, which also fixes `age()`.\n3. **`catalog/factory.py`**: `sample_books()` was missing `Emma`, the third book its docstring promises. I added it.\n4. **`catalog/fees.py:14`**: the fee was days late *plus* the daily rate. It's now days late *times* the rate.\n5. **`catalog/inventory.py:24`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns the last `n`, and an empty list when `n <= 0`. Without that check, `recent(0)` would have returned the whole history.\n6. **`catalog/members.py:4`**: the borrowing limit was 3, but the comment and tests say 5. I changed it to 5.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 51588, "requests_cache_write": 86122, "requests_cost_usd": 0.5400876, "reques